SCOPE
  Implemented the LiveSignalMonitor page natively in SwiftUI at full panel / state /
  string parity with the web source. The web page is a thin wrapper over
  `useLiveSignalStream` (SSE firehose, vehicle-scoped, tailMax 500) + `LiveSignalTail`
  (scrolling Time/Signal/Value/Type/Freshness table + 4 stat cards + filter / pause /
  auto-scroll / clear + connection badge). All reproduced SwiftUI-native (no web
  cloning): a titled header (vehicle picker + connected/disconnected badge) and the
  live tail panel with first-class loading / empty(waiting) / noMatch / error / stale
  states, bound through an @Observable model driven by the live SSE seam.

SHIPPED FILES (apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Telemetry/**)
  LiveSignalMonitorPage.swift          — View scaffold + LiveSignalMonitorStrings (catalog keys)
  LiveSignalMonitorPage.Support.swift  — value types + seams + in-memory source + LiveSignalMonitorCatalogKeys
  LiveSignalMonitorPage.Model.swift    — @Observable LiveSignalMonitorPageModel (P1/S8) — tail fold/cap/rate/state
  LiveSignalMonitorPage.Views.swift    — header, connection badge, tail panel, 4 stat cards, states
  LiveSignalMonitorPage.Rows.swift     — column header, signal row, kind badge/tint, freshness chip, formatters
  LiveSignalMonitorPage.Adapter.swift  — prod LiveStreamProvider<LiveFleetEvent> → seam bridge + route registration
  LiveSignalMonitorPage.Previews.swift — DEBUG previews (live / waiting / failed / stale) via in-memory source
  LiveSignalMonitorPage.Tests.swift    — 28 XCTest cases (@testable import), Swift 6 strict concurrency
