  Sources/App/AppRouteParser.swift     — "/live-monitor" → .telemetry deep-link alias (web /signals also → .telemetry)
  Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift           — chains LiveSignalMonitorRouteRegistration onto the route-host registry
  project.yml                          — adds TeslaSync/Features source path to both app targets (iOS + macOS)
LEDGER
  apps/parity/apple-ledger.json        — page:telemetry/LiveSignalMonitor rows (apple-ios, apple-macos) → done 4/4

ARCHITECTURE NOTES
  - Page/Model/Support/Views/Rows are Shared-FREE (Foundation/Observation/SwiftUI only): they build + unit-test
    under Swift 6 strict concurrency WITHOUT the KMP framework. The live data flows through the Shared-free
    `LiveSignalMonitorSource` seam (mirrors the P4 LiveControls `LiveControlsSource` pattern).
  - The production `LiveStreamMonitorSource` (Adapter.swift) is the ONLY page file touching the live-stream /
    shared-facade types (LiveStreamProvider/LiveFleetEvent/LiveScalar/LiveStreamTarget/LiveConnectionState). It
    bridges the real SSE firehose into the seam, filtering to the selected vehicle (web useLiveSignalStream scope).
  - Until the KMP SseClient is bootstrapped at the composition root, the page is wired with
    `LiveStreamProvider.unavailable()` — an HONEST connecting→offline provider that drives the loading→error/
    reconnect chrome (never fabricated rows; ADR-011). Swap for SharedLiveStreamProvider.live(client:tokenProvider:).
  - Strings: every visible literal resolves from Localizable.xcstrings; all 21 liveMonitor.* keys already exist
    in the catalog under the `translation.` namespace (the i18next default), so key names match web verbatim and
    the catalog itself was NOT edited.

